Kendall’s rank correlation can be interpreted exactly the same as Pearson’s correlation coefficient in terms of magnitude and valence. Kendall’s estimates, however, are often more conservative than Pearson’s (tau = -.77, r = -.85). Judging by either test, there is a significant strong negative correlation between engine volume (disp) and miles per gallon (mpg).
